11796	{"artifactId":"LLD-3c6a109dffcde0c1-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-3c6a109dffcde0c1-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-16T08:13:17.731Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The issue's fix intent is covered: the rule is defined once and shared like the scope rule, placed in the step prompts and the schema descriptions of the path-valued fields, a write-time check is considered (a2 chosen, a3 rejected with a reason), and existing records are not rewritten.","evidence":"ISSUE.md Fix intent asks for: one form, the rule in step prompts and in schema descriptions 'defined once and shared like the existing scope rule', to 'consider a write-time check', and 'existing records are not rewritten'. The LLD covers each: PATH_FORM_RULE (2.3), schema descriptions (3.2), checkPathForms (2.2), alternatives a1/a2/a3 (7), and Migration 'Data rewrite: no'. The issue's 'does not resolve from the root' option is weighed as a3 and rejected, and its limit is stated as an open question. [files: docs/standalone/write-project-file-references-relative-project-E202610163c6a109d/ISSUE.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the callSites schema at src/workflow/runners/design-story/schemas.ts:260 is a bare string array, and lld.ts:388 renders each call site as one code span.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts:388: `if (d.callSites.length > 0) { l.push('**Call sites:**'); for (const cs of d.callSites) l.push(`- \\`${cs}\\``); }`. The schema line (now :261) carries `callSites: { type: 'array', ... items: { type: 'string' } }`, and the description is the only addition. The issue quotes the bare form at :260 from before the build. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts, src/workflow/runners/design-story/schemas.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon's correction loop tests only for kind 'boundary', so a 'paths' failure takes the plain re-emit path. The in-session synthesize phase builds the error code as `synthesize-${kind}` and makes it retryable by default.","evidence":"src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:278 `failure.kind === 'boundary' && failure.correctable === true`. Otherwise it reaches :311 (throws only if retryable === false) and :318 `feedback = ...REJECTED: ${formatFailure(failure)}` (plain re-emit). src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:59 `const code = failure.ok ? 'synthesize-unknown' : `synthesize-${failure.kind}``, and :62 `failure.retryable ?? true`. [files: src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chat page links the :N, :N-M and :N:C line forms (CREF_CORE in vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-markup.ts).","evidence":"vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-markup.ts:21 `CREF_CORE='(...\\.(?:'+CREF_EXT+'))(?::(\\d+)(?:-\\d+)?(?::\\d+)?)?'`: :N, an optional -M and an optional :C. It requires a known extension, which matches the LLD's edge case 'extensionless file is not clickable'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-markup.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"PATH_FORM_RULE is defined once in the shared prompt fragments module beside ANTI_OVERREACH_RULE / SMALLEST_SHAPE_RULE and imported at each site. It is not a duplicate of an existing rule.","evidence":"src/workflow/runners/scope-prompts.ts:75 `export const PATH_FORM_RULE: string = ...` sits after SMALLEST_SHAPE_RULE (:61). A grep finds no definition elsewhere, only imports in orchestrator.ts:157, issue/index.ts:23, design-story/index.ts:30 and the define/design-epic/design-story/plan schemas.ts files. [files: src/workflow/runners/scope-prompts.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"validateBodyAndCitations (the reused hook) is the shared write-time validator that every synthesize path calls, so a check added there reaches all workflows.","evidence":"src/workflow/synthesizer.ts:207 defines it. src/workflow/orchestrator.ts calls it at :498, :744, :920, :1234, :1879, :2258, :2446 and :2702, covering stub, brainstorm, issue, define, design.epic, design.story (epic and standalone) and plan. [files: src/workflow/synthesizer.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding 'paths' to the ValidationFailure kind union breaks no consumer, because none switches exhaustively on kind. The change sites listed (synthesizer.ts, workflow-rpc.ts, workflow-step synthesize phase) are the consumers of kind.","evidence":"A grep for `.kind === 'schema'|'citations'`, `case 'citations'` and `Record<ValidationFailure['kind']` in src returns nothing. The only kind consumers are workflow-rpc.ts:278/292 (=== 'boundary') and synthesize.ts:59 (string template). synthesizer.ts:52 now reads `'schema' | 'citations' | 'boundary' | 'paths'`. [files: src/workflow/synthesizer.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The rule reaches every synthesize prompt in orchestrator.ts (stub, brainstorm, issue, define, design.epic, design.story, plan) and the step prompts and schemas that author callSites / pathsCited (define, design.epic, design.story, plan).","evidence":"orchestrator.ts interpolates PATH_FORM_RULE at :320, :627, :827, :978, :1480, :2026 and :2569 (7 synthesize prompts). pathsCited carries `description: PATH_FORM_RULE` in design-epic/schemas.ts:33, plan/schemas.ts:67, design-story/schemas.ts:33 and define/schemas.ts:85. callSites carries it at design-story/schemas.ts:261. The design.story step prompts carry it at design-story/index.ts:151 and :311, and the issue runner at issue/index.ts:55. [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts, src/workflow/runners/design-story/schemas.ts, src/workflow/runners/define/schemas.ts, src/workflow/runners/design-epic/schemas.ts, src/workflow/runners/plan/schemas.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design.story synthesize prompt's 'verbatim from s4' hard rule gets the stated exception for call sites.","evidence":"src/workflow/orchestrator.ts:2010: '- `body.contractDetails`, `body.dataModelChanges`, `body.interactionWithShared` MUST be verbatim from s4, except that every `callSites` entry is written in the form the file-reference rule below requires.' [files: src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"validateBodyAndCitations can pass meta.repoPath, because every artifact meta carries a string repoPath. The callSites are read from the stored LLD body field dataModelChanges[].callSites, with no shape change.","evidence":"src/workflow/types.ts:302 `ArtifactMetaBase { ... readonly repoPath: string; }`. src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts:84 `readonly callSites: readonly string[];` and :146 `readonly dataModelChanges: readonly DataModelChange[];`. synthesizer.ts:251-259 callSitesOf reads body.dataModelChanges[].callSites defensively, so it returns empty for a non-LLD body. [files: src/workflow/types.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts, src/workflow/synthesizer.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing records are not re-validated: the check runs only when a stage synthesizes a new artifact, so records already on disk that use the '::' symbol form or prose call sites keep loading and rendering.","evidence":"checkPathForms is called only from validateBodyAndCitations (synthesizer.ts:215), which runs only inside the orchestrator's finalize/synthesize paths. The artifact readers (e.g. lld.ts:492 isLld guard) do not call it. Stored records still carry the symbol form; for example .insrc/artifacts/LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1.json holds 10 `*.ts::Symbol` strings (the LLD says 13 across records; the exact count was not reconciled, and it does not bear on the design). [files: src/workflow/synthesizer.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A bad entry is detectable and the failure names each offending entry in details, which reaches the retry prompt. A persistent bad path ends at the existing retry limit, like a citations failure.","evidence":"synthesizer.ts:274-290 builds details per entry, for example `call site '${site}': ${problem}` and `citation ${c.id} (${c.kind}) ref ...`, and returns kind 'paths' with no retryable:false. workflow-rpc.ts:314-318 re-emits with `formatFailure(failure)` until `attempt === maxAttempts`, then throws 'synthesize rejected after N attempts'. In-session, synthesize.ts:62-63 returns a retryable 'synthesize-paths' error. [files: src/workflow/synthesizer.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The path check runs only after boundary and citation checks pass, so their results are unchanged for well-formed path fields.","evidence":"synthesizer.ts:211-215: boundary is checked first and returns early if not ok; validateCitations comes next and returns early if not ok; only then `return checkPathForms(...)`. [files: src/workflow/synthesizer.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac1 rule reaches prompts/schemas, ac2 bad entry refused and named, ac3 well-formed paths accepted and result unchanged) maps to named tests in src/workflow/__tests__/path-forms.test.ts.","evidence":"The LLD Acceptance mapping table lists tests for ac1, ac2 and ac3, all in src/workflow/__tests__/path-forms.test.ts, which exists in the repo (Glob). Test framework is node:test via tsx, per the CLAUDE.md test command. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/path-forms.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-16T08:13:17.731Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
